================================================================================
HKT UNIQUENESS AND THE MOND WALL
================================================================================

HOJMAN-KUCHAR-TEITELBOIM (1976): if H_perp (a) closes the Dirac algebra, (b) is ultralocal in
h_ij, (c) is at most quadratic in momenta, then H_perp IS GR's, uniquely.

COROLLARY (the MOND wall): exact MOND needs a nonlinear mu in the static constraint => H_perp
must be deformed => (a), (b), or (c) must break. Which one breaks DETERMINES which observable
fails. All six architectures tested:

  BREAKS              ARCHITECTURE                          FAILS AS                                EVIDENCE
  (a) algebra closure MMG: H_perp -> C_M                    gamma_PPN=0; alpha_3=-1                 8c53d66a
  (a) closure         MMG_REPAIR_A: S2'=D^2(q+lnN)          gamma=1 but alpha_3=-3, BTFR dies       2542182b
  (b) ultralocality   CGD nonlocal: E_i=D_i Delta^-1 (3)R   (3)R|_TT=0 => c_T=0                     6f603c50
  (b) ultralocality   DW: U=Box_ret^-1(R_uu)                ghost 2T+2S; Cassini 10-14 sigma        DOI 22132648
  (c) momentum struct F(A^2) kinetic carrier                khronon propagates (2+1)                sf40/sf41
  source routing      YCG: MOND on conformal q              sourced by T^i_i ~ 5e-7 rho => inert    5b7efd3d
  source routing      CMYG: g~=e^{2aq}g                     conformal=>no lensing; disformal=>cone  this run

THEOREM: {exact MOND, minimal coupling, 2 tensor DOF, gamma_PPN=1, c_T=1} is OVERDETERMINED.
GR is HKT's unique (a)+(b)+(c) point; MOND requires leaving it; every exit lands on a measured
contradiction. Not "MOND is impossible" -- rather: NO 2-DOF LOCAL DEFORMATION OF H_perp
DELIVERS MOND WITH GR'S LENSING. The wall is HKT, not any single construction.

MINIMAL SACRIFICE (priced from committed evidence):
 1. DROP "2 DOF" -> 2+1 with a SCREENED scalar (k-mouflage/Vainshtein). All gates become
    passable in principle: gamma_PPN=1 (screened), lensing OK (one conformal source =>
    Phi=Psi), c_T=1 (TT untouched), exact mu retained. COST: a third DOF.
    >>> THE ONLY DOOR WITH NO COMMITTED KILL. Repo status: "never tried, ranked #4". <<<
 2. DROP minimal coupling -> forbidden (and it is fitting, not deriving).
 3. DROP exact mu -> mu_n clears Cassini but does NOT repair gamma_PPN/alpha_3.
 4. DROP lensing/gamma=1 -> the theory stops describing the universe.

VERDICT: within {2 DOF, local, minimal, exact MOND, GR lensing} there is NO PASS. That set is
closed by HKT + six committed kills. The honest best-shot is 2+1 with a screened scalar --
a different, already-populated class, whose open gate is whether screening survives the
wide-binary/EFE data the DR4 registration tests.
